WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
Two receipts from the same café.

2
00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:05.560
The first says three
coffees and two cakes:

3
00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.400
thirteen pounds fifty.

4
00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.140
The second says two coffees and
three cakes: thirteen pounds.

5
00:00:12.190 --> 00:00:15.710
Every coffee costs the same,
and so does every cake.

6
00:00:15.760 --> 00:00:18.250
But the receipts only show totals.

7
00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.440
So how much is one cake?

8
00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:24.260
Is it just thirteen pounds
shared between five items?

9
00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:29.280
In this mission, you'll write each
receipt as an equation in two unknowns.

10
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:32.630
You'll see that one equation
alone has endless solutions,

11
00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.520
so you need two that
are both true at once.

12
00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:40.060
And you'll add or subtract the
equations to eliminate one unknown.

13
00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:43.080
Your mission: find the price of one cake.
